{"title":"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three distinct even positive integers are chosen between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36af3a317653fc5ff424093b4df40c2b4d5a6f5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> inclusive. What is the largest possible average of these three integers?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The three biggest distinct positive integers that are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> or less are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/73119f04d6ae5f6eb4afc8c9c946a5744a11be50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/7/367f6b15d47102fd8fdfc1bafed72c1daeadb35a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$96$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb5840b5de77a128ea3df2890bd38babc862df31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{100+98+96}{3} = \\boxed{98}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"168\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~Bradygho\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that the average of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers that form an arithmetic progression is the median of the numbers. Also, notice that to maximize the average of three numbers, we need to maximize the numbers themselves. Using these observations, it is obvious the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/4/034809d75d8171bda0ef23c4f5a91e27e4143953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{98}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Mathdreams\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems\">Other 2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Answer Key\">2021 JMPSC Accuracy Answer Key</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JMPSC_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"JMPSC Problems and Solutions\">All JMPSC Problems and Solutions</a></li></ol>\n<p>The problems on this page are copyrighted by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://jmpsc.org\">Junior Mathematicians' Problem Solving Competition</a>. <span class=\"mw-valign-middle\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:JMPSC.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/120px-JMPSC.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/180px-JMPSC.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/ab/JMPSC.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 202610170